# tools/al/ales_ring_mod_witness.rish -- the ring modulator: the tremolo's triangle carrier let cross zero (ALES75).
#
# Season: the Six-Season double-seat, Season C thread (Lotus - the creative suite) - waymark ALES - rung ALES75.
# Design read: active-designing/date/20260814/20260814-201937_fill-ales75-lotus-ring-modulator-bipolar-carrier.md
# Stands on: lotus/tremolo.rye (ALES74 -- the amplitude write this generalizes by removing the floor); lotus/chorus.rye (ALES71 -- the
# triangle-LFO driver `triangle_delay_at`, now the carrier); lotus/glide.rye (ALES70 -- `glide_scale`, 256 = unity); lotus/timeline.rye
# (ALES2 -- the Clip, sample_min/max, the one true saturate).
#
# lotus/ring_mod.rye is the tremolo with ONE restriction lifted -- the carrier is allowed to cross zero and go bipolar, flipping the sample's
# sign and scattering the spectrum into the ring modulator's metallic clang. It writes the tremolo's line verbatim,
# y[i] = saturate(x[i]-c(i)/glide_scale), and only widens the carrier's legal range from a one-sided attenuation (0 ≤ c ≤ scale) to a two-sided
# unit-bounded bipolar carrier (−scale ≤ c ≤ scale). The selftest proves the recognition outright: a NON-NEGATIVE CARRIER IS EXACTLY THE
# TREMOLO, matched sample-by-sample against the real tremolo; a hand-computed bipolar case (0 -> +1 -> 0 -> −1) shows the sign flip; a constant
# −unity carrier inverts; unity passthrough is exact; and the lone two's-complement corner (sample_min under a −unity carrier, −(−32768) =
# 32768) SATURATES to sample_max rather than wrapping -- the one place the ring modulator's saturate does real work the tremolo's never did; a
# period not a positive multiple of four refuses BadPeriod, a negative depth BadDepth, a carrier past unity either way BadCarrier, an
# out-of-range span BadRange. Purely local -- no delay line, no snapshot, no lookahead, no network, no keys, no funds, no real device, no sample rate.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/al/ales_ring_mod_witness.rish

say "ales-ring-mod: Language EN — ALES74's tremolo pointed the triangle LFO at the sample's amplitude and held the result to an ATTENUATION, so the voice was never louder than the dry and the write's saturate was a no-op. The RING MODULATOR is that rung with one restriction lifted: the carrier is allowed to CROSS ZERO and go negative. A carrier below zero flips the sample's sign; swung fast it multiplies the signal by a bipolar wave and scatters the spectrum into metallic sum-and-difference tones — the ring modulator's unmistakable clang, the tremolo's named sibling."
say "ales-ring-mod: Style Radiant — the law is stated positively as a family identity: a RING MODULATOR WHOSE CARRIER NEVER GOES NEGATIVE IS EXACTLY THE TREMOLO. It writes the tremolo's line verbatim, y[i] = saturate(x[i]·c(i)/glide_scale), and only widens the carrier's legal range from 0 ≤ c ≤ scale to a two-sided −scale ≤ c ≤ scale. In place with NO snapshot — every output depends only on its own input sample, the tremolo's thinnest discipline carried forward."
say "ales-ring-mod: Lens TAME — one clip of i16 PCM, a u32 span, the scaled bipolar carrier centre/depth, and a u32 period; the carrier is unit-bounded (|c| ≤ glide_scale), so the triangle and the multiply run in i64 and the write saturates once — a no-op EXCEPT the lone sample_min-inverted corner (−(−32768) = 32768 clamped to 32767), where the two's-complement asymmetry makes the saturate genuinely earn its keep; a period not a positive multiple of four (or past max_clip) refuses BadPeriod, a negative depth BadDepth, a carrier past unity in either direction BadCarrier, a span outside the samples BadRange, all before any write, the clip untouched on refusal; there is NO BadGain, NO BadDelay, NO BadLevel; siloed to lotus/, the carrier in scaled units and the period in samples, no delay line, no snapshot, no lookahead, no network, no keys, no funds, no device."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "lotus/bin/ring_mod"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p lotus/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/ring_mod.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "ales-ring-mod: build failed — ${build.err}"

let outfile = "lotus/bin/ring_mod.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "ales-ring-mod: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "ales-ring-mod: ${shown.out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN ales-ring-mod' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "ales-ring-mod: selftest did not print the GREEN ales-ring-mod line"
